B.hZ=new A.ph("Getting started",0,"gettingStarted")
B.hP=new A.aOe()
B.x=new A.x8(0,"everyone")
B.bll=new A.aP("The Wagon Structural Manager is the office side of the Wagon Inspector tablet app. Inspectors record cracks, damage and repairs against each wagon. The dashboard reads the same records and adds them up across your fleet.",B.x)
B.adA=new A.bV("What you are looking at",B.x)
B.b2D=s(["Your wagons come from the asset register. Each has a unit number, a model and a status: [[In-service]], [[Parked]] or [[Decommissioned]].","On the fleet pages every defect is shown in its latest recorded state. A crack found at one inspection and repaired at a later one counts as repaired, not as a current defect.","You see only the wagons your account has access to."],t.s)
B.a3g=new A.cD(B.b2D,B.x)
B.adG=new A.bV("What each page answers",B.x)
B.b3w=s(["[[Dashboard]]: what state is the fleet in right now?","[[Inspections]]: what has been inspected, and how far along is each inspection?","[[Current Defects]]: which defects are open, and how severe are they?","[[Hot Spots]]: which places on the wagon keep cracking?","[[Wagon Health]]: which wagons are in the worst condition?","[[Repaired]]: what has been repaired, and how?","[[Management]]: your wagons, your people and the rules your inspections follow."],t.s)
B.a37=new A.cD(B.b3w,B.x)
B.bi9=new A.ho("A decommissioned wagon is out of the fleet, so its defects leave the current counts: the Dashboard's defect cards, Current Defects, Hot Spots and Wagon Health. Its inspections stay on the Inspections page and its repairs on the Repaired page, because those are history.",B.x)
B.b7u=s([B.bll,B.adA,B.a3g,B.adG,B.a37,B.bi9],t.f)
B.bax=s(["start-navigation","start-roles","dashboard"],t.s)
B.afV=new A.dG("start-overview","What the dashboard is","The Wagon Structural Manager shows the condition of your wagon fleet as its inspections recorded it: which wagons have defects, how severe they are, where they sit on the wagon and what has been repaired.",B.hZ,B.hP,B.x,B.b7u,B.bax)
B.bl6=new A.aP("Three things move you around: the rail on the left, the numbers and rows on each page, and the panel that opens on the right.",B.x)
B.adX=new A.bV("The rail and the top bar",B.x)
B.bdk=s(["The rail lists the pages, and it is the same for everyone. The button at its top ([[Collapse navigation]]) shrinks it to icons.","The top bar shows the number of wagons in the register, the theme switch, the ? button for help, your name and [[Sign out]]. Your name opens [[My profile]].","The logo at the far left of the top bar is that of the company that owns the wagons on screen, once it has one."],t.s)
B.a3n=new A.cD(B.bdk,B.x)
B.aen=new A.bV("Numbers and rows are links",B.x)
B.b6z=s(["A number on a card opens the page that lists what it counted, already filtered to it.","A row opens that wagon, inspection or defect. A wagon opens full screen, and [[Back]] at the top left returns you. Inspections open in a panel on the right, which you shut with [[Close]].","In a table, a column heading sorts by that column."],t.s)
B.a2R=new A.cD(B.b6z,B.x)
B.aes=new A.bV("The model filter follows you",B.x)
B.bkt=new A.aP("The model chips, starting with [[All models]], narrow the fleet pages to one model, and a second row of chips to one of its components. The choice is shared: set it on one fleet page and the others stay on it, so that the pages never disagree about which wagons they count.",B.x)
B.b8S=s(["While a model is chosen, a pill with its name sits beside the page title. Its \u2715 ([[Show all models]]) clears the filter.","[[Reset filters]] appears whenever a page differs from how it first opened. It clears that page's own filters, search and sort, and the model filter with them."],t.s)
B.a3b=new A.cD(B.b8S,B.x)
B.bi4=new A.ho("If a page looks empty or its numbers look low, look for the model pill beside the page title first.",B.x)
B.co=new A.x8(3,"wqmsAdmin")
B.bkA=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you have the client switcher ([[Switch client]]) in place of the logo. It chooses one client or [[All clients]]. Switching clears the model filter, closes the side panel and returns every fleet page to how it first opened.",B.co)
B.aep=new A.bV("Getting help",B.x)
B.bbr=s(["The ? button in the top bar ([[Help for this page]]) opens help for the page you are on, or in Management for the tab you are on.","While an inspection or a defect is open in the panel on the right, the ? in that panel's bar opens help for what is open. A wagon's page has its own ? at the top right.","[[Help]], the last entry in the rail, opens the Help page: every topic, the [[FAQ]] and the [[Glossary]], with one search across them all.","[[Ask for help]] at the foot of a help topic takes you to [[User Support]], ready to write to the WQMS team."],t.s)
B.a2U=new A.cD(B.bbr,B.x)
B.d2=new A.x8(1,"editors")
B.bl2=new A.aP("The inspection workspace has its own ? beside the inspection's status ([[Help for the workspace]]). Help opened there has no [[Ask for help]].",B.d2)
B.baS=s([B.bl6,B.adX,B.a3n,B.aen,B.a2R,B.aes,B.bkt,B.a3b,B.bi4,B.bkA,B.aep,B.a2U,B.bl2],t.f)
B.bem=s(["start-overview","dashboard","wagon-page","defect-page","mgmt-support"],t.s)
B.afZ=new A.dG("start-navigation","Finding your way","The rail on the left opens each page, and the model filter you set on one page follows you to the others until you change it.",B.hZ,B.hP,B.x,B.baS,B.bem)
B.bli=new A.aP("Everyone who can sign in sees the same pages in the rail. Your role decides which buttons appear on them and which Management tabs you can edit. To check yours, open [[My profile]] from your name in the top bar: it shows your [[Role]] and [[Company]].",B.x)
B.ae6=new A.bV("The roles",B.x)
B.b9k=s(["[[Viewer]]: reads every page and can export an inspection's report, and changes nothing. The top bar shows [[View only]].","[[Reliability]]: can also start and work on inspections, which is where a repair is recorded. Reads the Management tabs.","[[Admin]]: with [[All sites]], can also invite and manage your company's people, add and rename sites, and edit the Asset Register, Scopes, Thresholds and Notifications. An Admin with chosen sites works on those sites' wagons and inspections only, and reads the Management tabs. Where a company still has the older Manager or Coordinator roles, they can edit the wagons, Scopes, Thresholds and Notifications too.","[[Inspector]]: works in the Wagon Inspector tablet app. A login that is only an inspector cannot sign in to the dashboard."],t.s)
B.a3_=new A.cD(B.b9k,B.x)
B.bkp=new A.aP("An Admin, a Reliability user and a Viewer have [[All sites]] or only the sites chosen for them. You see the wagons, inspections and defects of your sites only.",B.x)
B.bhX=new A.ho("Repair work done outside an inspection is recorded by a WQMS admin, on the defect's page.",B.x)
B.blS=new A.aP("In [[Management]], everyone who can sign in sees [[Asset Register]], [[Users]], [[Thresholds]], [[Notifications]], [[Scopes]] and [[User Support]]. A tab you cannot edit shows the same list without its add and edit controls.",B.x)
B.adZ=new A.bV("If your account is View only",B.x)
B.bl4=new A.aP("You can open every page, filter and search it, open any wagon, inspection or defect, and export an inspection's report. You do not get [[New inspection]] or the add and edit controls in Management. Two things you can always do: change your own details and password in [[My profile]], and send a request from [[User Support]]. If you need to change records, ask your company's admin for a different role: [[Users]] in Management shows who that is.",B.x)
B.aeq=new A.bV("What your account can change",B.d2)
B.blw=new A.aP("Your account is not View only. On [[Inspections]] you have [[New inspection]], and an inspection that is [[In progress]] opens in the workspace. Which Management tabs you can edit depends on your role.",B.d2)
B.cj=new A.x8(2,"companyAdmin")
B.blX=new A.aP("You manage users. In [[Users]] you can invite people, change their role, and deactivate or reactivate them. In [[Asset Register]] you can add and edit wagons and add and rename sites, and you can edit [[Scopes]], [[Thresholds]] and [[Notifications]].",B.cj)
B.blr=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you see every client. Management also shows you [[Clients]], [[Reference data]] and [[Client logos]], which no client role sees.",B.co)
B.beq=s([B.bli,B.ae6,B.a3_,B.bkp,B.bhX,B.blS,B.adZ,B.bl4,B.aeq,B.blw,B.blX,B.blr],t.f)
B.bc6=s(["start-signin","mgmt-users","mgmt-support","defect-page"],t.s)
B.afR=new A.dG("start-roles","What your role lets you do","Your role decides which Management tabs you see and what you can change; a View only account can look but not change anything.",B.hZ,B.hP,B.x,B.beq,B.bc6)
B.bkm=new A.aP("You sign in with your [[Email]] and [[Password]]. The dashboard keeps you signed in on that browser between visits. Press [[Sign out]] in the top bar to end the session.",B.x)
B.ael=new A.bV("Your first sign-in",B.x)
B.bbJ=s(["Open the link in your invite email.","On [[Set your password]], press [[Continue]].","Type a password of at least 8 characters, twice, and press [[Set password]]. You are then signed in."],t.s)
B.buN=new A.kq(B.bbJ,B.x)
B.bi5=new A.ho("If the page says the link has expired or was already used, ask your admin to resend the invite.",B.x)
B.ady=new A.bV("If you forget your password",B.x)
B.aIZ=s(["On the sign-in page, press [[Forgot password?]].","Enter your email and press [[Send reset link]].","Open the link in the email, press [[Continue]] and choose a new password."],t.s)
B.buS=new A.kq(B.aIZ,B.x)
B.bkH=new A.aP("The page gives the same answer whether or not the address has an account, so that it never tells a stranger who is registered. If no email arrives, check the address you typed.",B.x)
B.aeg=new A.bV("Your profile",B.x)
B.blm=new A.aP("Press your name in the top bar to open [[My profile]].",B.x)
B.b8F=s(["[[Your details]]: change your [[First name]], [[Last name]] and [[Phone]], then press [[Save details]]. Your email, role and company are shown but cannot be changed here.","[[Change password]]: enter your current password, then the new one twice. The new one needs at least 8 characters.","[[Send me a reset link]]: emails you a reset link instead, for when you do not remember your current password."],t.s)
B.a2P=new A.cD(B.b8F,B.x)
B.adN=new A.bV("If the dashboard will not let you in",B.x)
B.bay=s(["A login that is only an inspector is for the Wagon Inspector tablet app. Ask your admin if you need dashboard access.","A deactivated account cannot sign in. Your admin can reactivate it.","If you sign out in another tab of the same browser, this tab returns to the sign-in page as well."],t.s)
B.a2N=new A.cD(B.bay,B.x)
B.b3T=s([B.bkm,B.ael,B.buN,B.bi5,B.ady,B.buS,B.bkH,B.aeg,B.blm,B.a2P,B.adN,B.a2N],t.f)
B.b7N=s(["start-roles","mgmt-users","mgmt-support"],t.s)
B.ag8=new A.dG("start-signin","Signing in, passwords and your profile","You sign in with your email and password, a forgotten password is reset through a link sent to your email, and My profile holds your details and your password.",B.hZ,B.hP,B.x,B.b3T,B.b7N)
B.ji=new A.ph("Fleet pages",1,"fleet")
B.br9=new A.rH("dashboard")
B.blh=new A.aP("The Dashboard answers one question: what state is the fleet in right now? Every number opens the page that lists what it counted, already filtered.",B.x)
B.adV=new A.bV("How each card counts",B.x)
B.aDb=s(["[[Wagon Fleet]]: the model chips filter every card. The [[In-service]], [[Parked]] and [[Decommissioned]] boxes follow the model filter, and each opens the Asset Register on that status.","[[Inspected]]: the share of the fleet with at least one inspection. The total under it is in-service plus parked wagons. Decommissioned wagons are never in it, which is why it can be smaller than the register.","[[Current Defects]]: every defect that is open now, by [[Critical]], [[Severe]] and [[Minor]] (and None, in grey, while there is one). The bar shows how many are at each severity; click a part of it to open those defects. A missed defect, one that could not be re-inspected, counts at the severity it was last seen with. [[Stabilised]] counts current defects whose status is Stabilised: held, but still there. [[Wagons with defects]] counts wagons with at least one current defect.","[[Not Inspected]]: [[Wagons with areas not inspected]] counts wagons with a missed defect, a missed area, or a location marked not inspected at their latest inspection. [[Missed defects]] counts only the missed defects that still carry a severity, the ones inside Current Defects, so the two rows are different numbers.","[[Repaired or Stabilised]]: every repaired defect. [[Repaired]] is a full repair. [[Stabilised]] is a repair recorded with a stabilising action, such as a crack arrest. Each row opens the Repaired page on that kind.","[[Defect Location]]: current defects by place and severity. Click a row to go from Zone to Region to View. A View opens its crack map in Hot Spots, and a coloured segment opens Current Defects for that place and severity."],t.s)
B.a3h=new A.cD(B.aDb,B.x)
B.bhU=new A.ho("Defects on a decommissioned wagon are in none of these counts except [[Repaired or Stabilised]], which is history.",B.x)
B.bex=s([B.blh,B.adV,B.a3h,B.bhU],t.f)
B.b68=s(["defects","health","hotspots","repairs","mgmt-registers"],t.s)
B.afS=new A.dG("dashboard","Dashboard","The Dashboard is your fleet at a glance: how many wagons there are and how many are inspected, the current defects by severity, what was not inspected, what has been repaired, and where on the wagon the defects sit.",B.ji,B.br9,B.x,B.bex,B.b68)
B.brd=new A.rH("inspections")
B.bkq=new A.aP("Inspections answers: what has been inspected, when, and how far along is each inspection? There is one row per inspection, newest first.",B.x)
B.adT=new A.bV("Reading the table",B.x)
B.bdU=s(["[[Unit]], [[Date]], [[Title]] and [[Scope]] say which wagon was inspected, when, and against which scope.","[[Defects]] is the same Defects number the inspection's own page shows. Damage, not-inspected and repaired items are counted separately there.","[[Status]] is how far along the inspection is: [[Draft]], [[In progress]], [[Scope complete]], [[Inspection complete]] or [[Published]].","Click a column heading to sort by it."],t.s)
B.a3e=new A.cD(B.bdU,B.x)
B.xq=new A.bV("Filtering",B.x)
B.bc7=s(["Each status chip shows how many inspections are at that status. Click one to list only those, and [[All inspections]] to list them all again.","The search box matches the title, the unit number and the job reference.",u.cD,"[[Reset filters]] puts the page back to how it first opened, including the model filter."],t.s)
B.a2S=new A.cD(B.bc7,B.x)
B.aeb=new A.bV("Opening an inspection",B.x)
B.blC=new A.aP("Click a row to open the inspection in the panel on the right, with its details, its defects and its [[Report]].",B.x)
B.adQ=new A.bV("Starting an inspection",B.d2)
B.b6n=s(["Press [[New inspection]].","Choose the site if there is more than one, then the wagon, then the scope.","Check the [[Title]] and the [[Inspection date]], then press [[Create & open]]."],t.s)
B.buV=new A.kq(B.b6n,B.d2)
B.blA=new A.aP("The new inspection opens straight in the workspace. Later, an inspection that is [[In progress]] has an [[Open workspace]] button at the end of its row.",B.d2)
B.b7R=s([B.bkq,B.adT,B.a3e,B.xq,B.a2S,B.aeb,B.blC,B.adQ,B.buV,B.blA],t.f)
B.bbk=s(["inspection-page","workspace","mgmt-scopes"],t.s)
B.afM=new A.dG("inspections","Inspections","Inspections lists every inspection with its status; the status counts filter the table, and a row opens that inspection.",B.ji,B.brd,B.x,B.b7R,B.bbk)
B.bra=new A.rH("defects")
B.bkf=new A.aP("Current Defects answers: which defects are open on the fleet now, and how severe is each one? With no filter set, the count beside the title is the same number as the Dashboard's Current Defects card.",B.x)
B.aek=new A.bV("What is on the list",B.x)
B.bcK=s(["Every defect that is not repaired and was not found clear at a later inspection.","A missed defect, one that could not be re-inspected, stays on the list while it carries the severity it was last seen with, because the crack is still on the wagon. Its [[Status]] reads [[Missed]].","Repaired defects are not here. They are on the Repaired page.","Defects on a decommissioned wagon are not here either."],t.s)
B.a3l=new A.cD(B.bcK,B.x)
B.FX=new A.bV("Reading a row",B.x)
B.bcQ=s(["[[Defect]] is the defect's id, the wagon's unit number then its number on that wagon (for example 57408L-3), and [[Location]] says where on the wagon it is.","[[Data]] is the defect's code, such as S50LF12 for a crack or D-Wear for a damage.","[[Severity]] is [[Critical]], [[Severe]] or [[Minor]], or None for a damage or an access structure that is not graded. The list opens worst first, None last.","[[Status]] is the defect's latest recorded status: [[New]], [[Grown]], [[No change]], [[Stabilised]] or [[Missed]].","[[Inspection]] is the inspection that first recorded the defect, with its date."],t.s)
B.a2Q=new A.cD(B.bcQ,B.x)
B.b5N=s(["The severity and status chips each show a count. Pick as many as you like in each group.","Under Location, click a bar to narrow the list to that Zone, then Region, then View. [[Clear location]] takes that narrowing off.","The unit box matches part of a unit number.","On a narrower window the filters sit above the table, and a button in the page header hides them ([[Hide filters]]) or shows them again ([[Show filters]]).","[[Reset filters]] clears all of these and the model filter."],t.s)
B.a36=new A.cD(B.b5N,B.x)
B.adS=new A.bV("Opening a defect",B.x)
B.blT=new A.aP("Click a row to open the defect on a full page, with its photos, its place on the drawing and its history. [[Previous defect]] and [[Next defect]] walk the list in the order you had it on screen.",B.x)
B.b8n=s([B.bkf,B.aek,B.a3l,B.FX,B.a2Q,B.xq,B.a36,B.adS,B.blT],t.f)
B.beb=s(["defect-page","repairs","hotspots","dashboard"],t.s)
B.afW=new A.dG("defects","Current Defects","Current Defects lists every defect that is open on the fleet now, with filters for model, severity, status, location and unit; repaired defects are on the Repaired page.",B.ji,B.bra,B.x,B.b8n,B.beb)
B.brc=new A.rH("hotspots")
B.bki=new A.aP("Hot Spots answers: which places on the wagon keep cracking? It ranks the drawing views by how many defects are recorded on each, and opens the crack map of the view you pick.",B.x)
B.pO=new A.bV("Reading the page",B.x)
B.bcL=s(["The two cards at the top and the [[Defect Location]] bars count the way the Dashboard does.","Under [[Hot Spots]], each tile is one view of one model, so the same place on two models is two tiles. [[Total]], [[Active]] and [[Repaired]] choose what the tiles count and re-rank them.","You see the ten highest. When there are more, press **Show all \u2026 locations** under the tiles to see the rest, and [[Show top 10]] to fold them away again."],t.s)
B.a30=new A.cD(B.bcL,B.x)
B.adC=new A.bV("Why a tile can differ from the Dashboard",B.x)
B.bm5=new A.aP("A tile is counted with the rule its crack map uses to draw pins. [[Active]] is every defect on that view that has not been repaired, and that includes every missed defect, whatever it was last seen as. The Dashboard counts a missed defect only while it still carries a severity. [[Repaired]] on a tile also includes prior repairs marked on the view. Defects found clear at a later inspection are on neither. The difference is deliberate: the Dashboard reports severity, and a tile reports what is marked on the drawing.",B.x)
B.ae2=new A.bV("The crack map",B.x)
B.b9r=s(["Click a tile, or a View row in [[Defect Location]], to open that view with one pin for each defect across the fleet.","[[View]] switches to another view of the same model. The number after each name is how many pins it has.","The status chips ([[New]], [[Grown]], [[No Change]], [[Missed]], [[Stabilised]], [[Repaired]]) all start on. Click one to hide those pins.","Click a pin to read that defect, or a group of pins to list only the defects in it. [[View defect details]] opens the full page.","The [[Hot Spots]] link above the title goes back to the ranking."],t.s)
B.a3f=new A.cD(B.b9r,B.x)
B.b3X=s([B.bki,B.pO,B.a30,B.adC,B.bm5,B.ae2,B.a3f],t.f)
B.b2B=s(["dashboard","defects","defect-page"],t.s)
B.ag2=new A.dG("hotspots","Hot Spots","Hot Spots shows which places on the wagon keep cracking, ranked, and opens the crack map for the place you pick.",B.ji,B.brc,B.x,B.b3X,B.b2B)
B.brb=new A.rH("health")
B.bkF=new A.aP("Wagon Health answers: which wagons are in the worst condition? There is one row for each wagon that has at least one inspection, worst first. Decommissioned wagons are left out.",B.x)
B.adK=new A.bV("The counts beside the title",B.x)
B.bkN=new A.aP("They describe the fleet, not the rows on screen, so they change with the model filter and not with the search box or the chips. The first is every wagon that is not decommissioned, inspected or not. The count **with defects** is the wagons with at least one current defect, and **not fully inspected** is the wagons that carry the [[Not inspected]] mark described below.",B.x)
B.bc3=s(["[[Most Severe]] is the wagon's worst current defect: its severity and that defect's status. Where two defects share the worst severity, a grown one is shown before a new one.","[[Critical]], [[Severe]] and [[Minor]] count the wagon's current defects at each severity. A missed defect counts at the severity it was last seen with.","[[Current]] counts the open defects that are not missed, so the three severity columns can add up to more than it.","[[Repaired]] counts the wagon's repaired defects.","[[Not inspected]] shows a warning mark when the wagon has a missed defect, a missed area, or a location marked not inspected at its latest inspection.","[[Last inspection]] is the date of the wagon's most recent inspection."],t.s)
B.a3s=new A.cD(B.bc3,B.x)
B.adJ=new A.bV("Filtering and opening",B.x)
B.b8T=s(["[[With defects]] keeps only wagons with a current defect. [[Not inspected]] keeps only wagons with the warning mark.","The search box matches part of a unit number, and every column heading sorts.","Click a row to open the wagon's page full screen, with its defects and its past inspections."],t.s)
B.a2X=new A.cD(B.b8T,B.x)
B.bi8=new A.ho("You cannot change a wagon's status here or on the wagon's page. Status is changed in Management, Asset Register, so that a stray click while you are reading cannot decommission a wagon.",B.x)
B.b9M=s([B.bkF,B.adK,B.bkN,B.FX,B.a3s,B.adJ,B.a2X,B.bi8],t.f)
B.bcW=s(["wagon-page","dashboard","mgmt-registers"],t.s)
B.ag7=new A.dG("health","Wagon Health","Wagon Health has one row for each inspected wagon, worst first, and a row opens that wagon.",B.ji,B.brb,B.x,B.b9M,B.bcW)
B.bre=new A.rH("repairs")
B.blx=new A.aP("Repaired answers: what has been repaired, on which wagon, and how? It lists every defect whose status is Repaired, grouped by wagon.",B.x)
B.adY=new A.bV("Repaired and Stabilised on this page",B.x)
B.b83=s(["[[Repaired]] is a full repair.","[[Stabilised]] is a repair recorded with a stabilising action: **Crack Arrest**, **Ground out** or **Temporary Repair**. It is drawn as a green ring, where a full repair is a green disc.","[[All]] shows both."],t.s)
B.a2H=new A.cD(B.b83,B.x)
B.bi_=new A.ho("A defect whose status is still Stabilised is not on this page. It is a current defect, because the crack is held but still there. Find it on Current Defects under the Stabilised status.",B.x)
B.FW=new A.bV("Reading the list",B.x)
B.ber=s(["Each group heading shows the unit, its model and how many repaired defects it has. Click the heading to fold the group away or open it again.","Each row shows the defect's code, the location, the action taken and the date of the inspection that recorded the repair.","A decommissioned wagon's repairs stay on this page, because the page is history."],t.s)
B.a3q=new A.cD(B.ber,B.x)
B.bbP=s(["The second row of chips lists the actions that belong to the kind you chose. Pick one or more to see only those repairs.",u.cD,"[[Reset filters]] clears the chips and the model filter, and opens every group again."],t.s)
B.a2Y=new A.cD(B.bbP,B.x)
B.aec=new A.bV("Opening a repair",B.x)
B.blR=new A.aP("Click a row to open the defect on a full page, with its photos and its history. [[Previous defect]] and [[Next defect]] walk the rows you can see, skipping any group you folded away.",B.x)
B.b9N=s([B.blx,B.adY,B.a2H,B.bi_,B.FW,B.a3q,B.xq,B.a2Y,B.aec,B.blR],t.f)
B.b9I=s(["defect-page","defects","dashboard"],t.s)
B.afO=new A.dG("repairs","Repaired","Repaired lists every repaired defect, grouped by wagon, and separates full repairs from stabilising repairs.",B.ji,B.bre,B.x,B.b9N,B.b9I)
B.mH=new A.ph("Wagons, inspections and defects",2,"drill")
B.bm0=new A.aP("A wagon's page answers: what is this wagon, what condition is it in now, and what has been recorded against it? It opens full screen when you click a wagon, for example a row in [[Wagon Health]] or [[Open]] on a row of the Asset Register. [[Back]] at the top left returns you to where you were.",B.x)
B.bef=s(["The unit number is in the bar at the top. Below it: the wagon's asset (model and component), its site, the date of its last inspection and its status, then its current defects counted at each severity. A missed defect counts at the severity it was last seen with. **Repaired** counts its repaired defects, and [[Not inspected]] shows while a defect or an area on the wagon is still missed.","The cards are the Dashboard's own, counting this wagon only: [[Current Defects]], [[Not Inspected]] (its [[Locations not inspected]], [[Areas not inspected]] and [[Missed defects]]), [[Repaired or Stabilised]], and [[Defect Location]], which shows where on the wagon its current defects are. On a narrow screen the cards stack.","[[Defects]]: every defect recorded on the wagon, repaired ones included, worst first. Each row shows the defect's symbol (its shape is the status, its colour the severity), its defect number (for example **57408L-2**: the wagon's unit number, then the defect's number on that wagon), its code, where it is, and the date of the latest inspection that recorded that code. A missed defect keeps the date of the inspection that last saw it.","[[Not Inspected]]: what is still not inspected on the wagon as of its latest inspection, whichever inspection recorded it, in up to three lists: [[Locations not inspected]], [[Areas not inspected]] and [[Missed defects]]. An inspection still in [[Draft]] is not used, because nobody has started it. The section is absent when there is nothing to list.","[[Past inspections]]: every inspection of this wagon, newest first, with its date, scope and status.","[[Asset]]: the wagon's register record, with its status beside the heading. A field with nothing recorded is left out."],t.s)
B.a34=new A.cD(B.bef,B.x)
B.adw=new A.bV("What you can click",B.x)
B.ak8=s(["A defect opens full screen, where the arrows at the top right step through the wagon's other defects.","A number on a card, or a bar of [[Defect Location]], opens the defects it counted full screen, one after another. Those links stay on this wagon.","A past inspection opens that inspection's page in a panel on the right, and so does a row under [[Not Inspected]]. [[Close]] shuts the panel and leaves you on the wagon.","[[Report]] at the top opens the report of the wagon's latest inspection. The PDF icon at the end of a past inspection opens that inspection's report."],t.s)
B.a3i=new A.cD(B.ak8,B.x)
B.bhW=new A.ho("A wagon's status cannot be changed on this page. It changes only in Management, on the Asset Register.",B.x)
B.bl_=new A.aP("A wagon that has never been inspected shows [[Never inspected]] for its last inspection, [[No defects recorded]] and [[No inspections yet]].",B.x)
B.blg=new A.aP("In [[All clients]], two clients can have wagons with the same unit number, so the page names the client under it. An old link to a shared number asks you to [[Choose a wagon]].",B.co)
B.b6U=s([B.bm0,B.pO,B.a34,B.adw,B.a3i,B.bhW,B.bl_,B.blg],t.f)
B.b3K=s(["health","inspection-page","defect-page","mgmt-registers"],t.s)
B.afX=new A.dG("wagon-page","A wagon's page","A wagon's page fills the screen: the wagon's own Dashboard cards, its defects with the date each was last recorded, what its latest inspection could not inspect, its past inspections and its register details.",B.mH,B.hP,B.x,B.b6U,B.b3K)
B.bm6=new A.aP("An inspection's page answers: what did this inspection cover, how far along is it, and what did it record? It opens in the panel on the right from a row on [[Inspections]] or from a wagon's [[Past inspections]].",B.x)
B.b4O=s(["[[Asset]] and [[Details]]: the wagon, the inspection date, and the scope with how many of the model's views it covers.","Four counts of what this inspection recorded. [[Defects]] counts cracks and access-structure findings, and [[Damage]] counts damage. A finding this inspection missed or repaired is counted under [[Not inspected]] or [[Repaired]] instead. [[Not inspected]] also counts the locations it marked.","[[Locations not inspected]]: the locations this inspection marked, each with its reason.","[[Defects]]: every defect this inspection observed, whether it found it or updated one found earlier. A row opens the defect."],t.s)
B.a3o=new A.cD(B.b4O,B.x)
B.bi1=new A.ho("The page shows what this inspection saw. Each defect has the status and severity this inspection recorded, not its latest ones. If a later inspection finds the crack grown or repairs it, this page and its report do not change. The exception is repair work recorded outside an inspection: it is added to the defect's latest inspection, published or not, and that inspection's page and report then show the repair. For the defect as it is now, open it from [[Current Defects]].",B.x)
B.adO=new A.bV("The report",B.x)
B.b3x=s(["[[Report]] opens a preview of the inspection's PDF. [[Download PDF]] saves it and [[Print]] prints it.","For some of the defects only, press [[Select defects]], tick the rows you want and press **Report selected**. [[Select defects]] appears when there is more than one defect."],t.s)
B.a2T=new A.cD(B.b3x,B.x)
B.adI=new A.bV("Moving the inspection on",B.d2)
B.blD=new A.aP("The [[ACTIONS]] box offers the next step for the inspection's status.",B.d2)
B.bej=s(["[[Draft]]: [[Start inspection]].","[[In progress]]: [[Open workspace]], where it is recorded, and [[Mark scope complete]].","[[Scope complete]]: [[Mark inspection complete]]. [[Inspection complete]]: [[Publish]].","[[Edit]] changes the title, the references and the dates. The scope's views can be changed until the scope is completed, and the unit until a defect is recorded.","[[Reopen]] returns a [[Scope complete]] or [[Inspection complete]] inspection to In progress. Its completion is cleared until it is completed again."],t.s)
B.a3a=new A.cD(B.bej,B.d2)
B.bia=new A.ho("[[Publish]] on this page does not ask for a sign-off: the sign-off is a step of the workspace's [[Complete]] tab. Like the workspace's [[Publish inspection]], it first shows who will be emailed: [[Notification will go to:]] lists the people told automatically, and [[Also notify (optional):]] lets you tick others and add a comment.",B.d2)
B.blG=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you can also [[Reopen]] a published inspection. Its sign-off is cleared, and it has to be completed and published again.",B.co)
B.bb2=s([B.bm6,B.pO,B.a3o,B.bi1,B.adO,B.a2T,B.adI,B.blD,B.a3a,B.bia,B.blG],t.f)
B.bek=s(["inspections","defect-page","workspace","wagon-page"],t.s)
B.ag5=new A.dG("inspection-page","An inspection's page","An inspection's page shows the inspection's details, its status and its defects, and opens its report.",B.mH,B.hP,B.x,B.bb2,B.bek)
B.bky=new A.aP("A defect's page answers: what is this defect, where is it on the wagon, and how has it changed from one inspection to the next?",B.x)
B.adL=new A.bV("Two ways it opens",B.x)
B.bdQ=s(["From a table or a wagon's [[Defects]] list it opens full screen. [[Previous defect]] and [[Next defect]], or the left and right arrow keys, walk the list you came from.","From an inspection's page or a wagon's [[Not Inspected]] list it opens in the panel on the right, where [[Open full view]] shows it full screen and [[Report]] opens a PDF of this defect alone, as this page shows it."],t.s)
B.a3m=new A.cD(B.bdQ,B.x)
B.aRe=s(["At the top: the defect's code, then the severity and the status.","**Growth since last inspection** appears when the status is [[Grown]] and this observation and the one before it both carry a length.","[[Below suggested severity]]: the defect is graded lower than its thresholds suggest. It says which severity is suggested and where from, and the reason when the inspector chose the lower grade on purpose.","[[Photos]]: every photo of the defect, newest first, each with the date of the inspection that took it. Click a photo to open it full screen, then use the arrows at the sides (or the left and right arrow keys) to move to the previous or next photo, and **Esc** or the close button to leave. A photo that cannot be downloaded shows **This photo couldn't be loaded.**","[[Crack map]]: the view the defect sits on, with a pin where it is.","[[Location]]: its Zone, Region and View.","[[Linked defect]]: shown when a stabilised crack has cracked again. In the panel on the right, the row opens the other defect.","[[History]]: one row per observation, oldest first. Click a row for what was recorded and its photos, and [[Open inspection]] for the inspection that recorded it."],t.s)
B.a35=new A.cD(B.aRe,B.x)
B.aed=new A.bV("Opened from an inspection",B.x)
B.bl5=new A.aP("The top of the page then shows what that inspection recorded, and its rows in [[History]] are marked [[This inspection]]. [[Photos]] still holds every photo of the defect, each with its date.",B.x)
B.ae7=new A.bV("Recording repair work",B.x)
B.blz=new A.aP("Repair work is recorded during an inspection, when the defect is updated as [[Repaired]] or [[Stabilised]]. Repair work done outside an inspection is recorded by a WQMS admin.",B.x)
B.bkS=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you record it on this page with [[Mark repaired\u2026]] and [[Mark stabilised\u2026]]. The repair is added to the defect's latest inspection.",B.co)
B.b34=s(["[[Mark repaired\u2026]]: choose the [[Action taken]], add a comment or a photo if you have one, and press [[Mark repaired]].","[[Mark stabilised\u2026]]: choose the [[Action taken]], attach the required photo and press [[Continue]], then choose the severity after stabilisation.","A repaired defect offers neither, and a stabilised one only [[Mark repaired\u2026]].","On a prior repair or an area that was not inspected, [[Mark repaired\u2026]] cannot be pressed. Point at it to read why: [[Not a repairable defect.]]","Neither is offered on a defect opened from a published inspection: open it from [[Current Defects]] instead."],t.s)
B.a39=new A.cD(B.b34,B.co)
B.blB=new A.aP("In the panel, [[Add photo]] attaches an image from your computer.",B.d2)
B.blb=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you may also see [[Update status\u2026]] in the panel. It reopens the defect's latest inspection, clearing its sign-off, and opens the workspace on the defect. While that inspection is in progress it reads [[Update in workspace]].",B.co)
B.b6_=s([B.bky,B.adL,B.a3m,B.pO,B.a35,B.aed,B.bl5,B.ae7,B.blz,B.bkS,B.a39,B.blB,B.blb],t.f)
B.beQ=s(["defects","inspection-page","wagon-page","mgmt-thresholds","mgmt-support"],t.s)
B.ag4=new A.dG("defect-page","A defect's page","A defect's page shows what the defect is and where it sits on the wagon, with its history of observations and its photos.",B.mH,B.hP,B.x,B.b6_,B.beQ)
B.bl1=new A.aP("The workspace is where you record an inspection. It opens when you create an inspection, and from [[Open workspace]] on one that is [[In progress]]. [[Inspections]] at the top left returns to the dashboard.",B.x)
B.ae9=new A.bV("The five tabs",B.x)
B.bdI=s(["[[Summary]]: the same details, counts and defect list as the inspection's page.","[[Capture]]: pick a Zone, a Region, then a View. Press [[Add Data]], click the drawing where the defect is, fill in the form and press [[Save defect]]. A pin opens its defect.","[[Prior]]: the wagon's defects from earlier inspections that this one has not updated yet. Open each and say what you found: [[Grown]], [[No change]], [[Stabilised]], [[Repaired]] or [[Missed]]. A crack stabilised earlier offers [[Re-cracked]] in place of [[Grown]] and [[Stabilised]].","[[Missed]]: locations, areas and cracks that earlier inspections could not inspect, each to be updated. [[Mark area]] records a place this inspection could not inspect, and why.","[[Complete]]: the checklist that finishes the inspection."],t.s)
B.a2I=new A.cD(B.bdI,B.x)
B.adH=new A.bV("Severity on a crack",B.x)
B.blH=new A.aP("As you fill in a crack, the form suggests its severity. Once it has the location type, crack type, depth and length, the line under **Severity** reads, for example, **Suggested Severe \xb7 from QHCH Master matrix**, and that severity is filled in for you. The suggestion comes from the severity matrix for the wagon's asset type, or from a specific threshold where one covers that part of the wagon.",B.x)
B.be3=s(["Keep it, or choose another severity. A higher one needs nothing more, and [[Use suggested]] puts the suggestion back.","A lower one opens [[Reason for lower severity]]: give a short reason before you save. It is saved with the defect as the first line of its comments, and a defect still graded below the suggestion shows it on its page under [[Below suggested severity]].","The length is the max length for L, T, I and M cracks (the total length when there is no max length) and the total length for X. A crack that re-cracked after a crack arrest is graded on its length plus the arrested length.","Non-structural cracks are never suggested: the form says to choose the severity yourself, Minor for cracked, Severe for broken and Critical for loss of function.","Where no matrix or specific threshold covers the crack, or the wagon's asset type has none yet, nothing is suggested and you choose the severity as before.","A damage or an access structure can also be graded **None**: it is recorded and shown on the wagon, in grey, but it is not graded Minor, Severe or Critical, and a crack cannot be None. Nothing is suggested for it."],t.s)
B.a3p=new A.cD(B.be3,B.x)
B.blN=new A.aP("A crack you update as [[Grown]] starts on its earlier severity and, once you change its length, follows the suggestion when it is the same or higher. A crack that grew is never lowered for you: a lower suggestion is shown with [[Use suggested]], and a severity lower than the earlier one, or than the suggestion, needs a reason, also when you edit that update later. When you edit a saved defect, its severity and reason stay as they were until you change them or a crack measurement.",B.x)
B.adB=new A.bV("A defect's photos",B.x)
B.ble=new A.aP("When you open a defect in the workspace, **PHOTOS** shows the photos this inspection took of it. When it has taken none yet, it shows the defect's latest photos under **Latest photos** and their date. **No photos yet** means the defect has none at all. Click a photo to open it full screen and step through the others with the arrows at the sides.",B.x)
B.adD=new A.bV("Finishing an inspection",B.x)
B.blL=new A.aP("On [[Complete]], each step unlocks when the one before is done.",B.x)
B.b4d=s(["[[Scope confirmation]]: [[Confirm scope complete]] is offered once nothing is left on [[Prior]] and [[Missed]].","[[Photo check]]: every New, Grown, No change and Stabilised defect needs a photo ([[Add photo]]) or a reason for having none ([[Bypass with reason]]). Then press [[Confirm photos]].","[[Sign-off]]: choose the [[Reliability user]], draw the signature with the mouse and press [[Sign off]].","[[Publish]]: [[Publish inspection]] publishes it, and recording in the workspace ends."],t.s)
B.buM=new A.kq(B.b4d,B.x)
B.bhZ=new A.ho("Finish the four steps in one visit. Once the scope is confirmed the inspection is no longer [[In progress]], so [[Open workspace]] is not offered for it. To come back, press [[Reopen]] on the inspection's page, which clears its completion.",B.x)
B.ae4=new A.bV("Who is told when you publish",B.x)
B.bkx=new A.aP("When the wagon's owner has set people up in [[Notifications]], [[Publish inspection]] first shows who will be told. [[Notification will go to:]] lists the people who are emailed automatically, each with the severity they are told about and how many of this inspection's defects that covers. [[Also notify (optional):]] lists the people you can choose to email as well. Nobody on it is ticked to begin with: tick the ones you want, and add a message for them in [[Comment for the email (optional)]].",B.x)
B.bb5=s(["Only a new defect, a defect that has grown, or one at a higher severity than before is reported. When none of them reaches anyone's level, the dialog says that no one is notified automatically.","A person marked **No email address** can still be ticked, but nothing is sent to them until an address is added in [[Users]].","You can tick up to 50 people, and the comment can be up to 1000 characters.","The emails are sent after you publish, and Cancel sends nothing. When no one is set up for the wagon's owner, the dialog is just the question."],t.s)
B.a2O=new A.cD(B.bb5,B.x)
B.ae0=new A.bV("Scope",B.x)
B.blW=new A.aP("The inspection's scope sets which views it covers. On Capture, a view outside it is dimmed and tagged **Not in scope**; it still opens. Prior and Missed are not limited by scope: a defect carried from an earlier inspection is listed wherever it sits and has to be updated before the scope can be confirmed.",B.x)
B.adW=new A.bV("What is locked, and when",B.x)
B.b3N=s(["A [[Draft]] has not been started: only [[Summary]] opens, and the other tabs answer [[Open the inspection first]].","[[Add Data]] works only while the inspection is [[In progress]]. After the scope is confirmed, [[Reopen inspection for corrections]] takes it back.","A [[Published]] inspection shows [[Summary]] alone, marked [[Read-only]]."],t.s)
B.a2L=new A.cD(B.b3N,B.x)
B.blM=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you have [[Reopen (admin)]] on a published inspection. It clears the sign-off.",B.co)
B.b9A=s([B.bl1,B.ae9,B.a2I,B.adH,B.blH,B.a3p,B.blN,B.adB,B.ble,B.adD,B.blL,B.buM,B.bhZ,B.ae4,B.bkx,B.a2O,B.ae0,B.blW,B.adW,B.a2L,B.blM],t.f)
B.b5Z=s(["inspections","inspection-page","mgmt-scopes","mgmt-users"],t.s)
B.ag3=new A.dG("workspace","The inspection workspace","The inspection workspace is where you record an inspection on screen, in five tabs: Summary, Capture, Prior, Missed and Complete.",B.mH,B.hP,B.d2,B.b9A,B.b5Z)
B.fa=new A.ph("Management",3,"management")
B.bgv=new A.m2("registers")
B.bku=new A.aP("Asset Register answers: which wagons do we have, what status is each in, and at which sites are they kept? [[Wagons]] and [[Sites]] switch between the two lists. Your company's Admin with [[All sites]] adds and edits both lists; where a company still has the older Manager or Coordinator roles, they can add and edit wagons too. Everyone else reads them.",B.x)
B.ae5=new A.bV("Wagons",B.x)
B.aJ2=s(["Wagons are grouped by model. Each row shows the [[Unit]], its site and company, and its [[Status]]: [[In-service]], [[Parked]] or [[Decommissioned]].","The status chips filter the list and count the wagons at each status. The search box finds a unit number.","A row, or [[Open]] on it, opens the wagon's page full screen.","A status box on the Dashboard's [[Wagon Fleet]] card opens this list on that status and on the model you had chosen. [[Reset filters]] clears both."],t.s)
B.a2F=new A.cD(B.aJ2,B.x)
B.aer=new A.bV("Adding and editing wagons",B.cj)
B.bdg=s(["[[Add wagon]]: enter the [[Unit no]], choose the [[Model - Component]] and the [[Status]], and the [[Site]] if there is more than one, then press [[Add]]. Two wagons at one site cannot share a unit number.","[[Import CSV]] adds many wagons at once. Choose a file and read the preview: each row is marked [[Add]], [[Skip]] (already in the register) or [[Error]], with the reason, such as a model that is not an active wagon type. Nothing is written until you press [[Commit]].","[[Edit]] changes the unit number, the component, the status and the serial number. The model and the site cannot be changed.","[[Change status]] moves a wagon between the three statuses."],t.s)
B.a31=new A.cD(B.bdg,B.cj)
B.bhY=new A.ho("A wagon's component locks once the wagon has an inspection or is listed in a scope, because an inspection keeps the views it was made on. The Edit drawer then shows it with a padlock and the reason.",B.cj)
B.ae1=new A.bV("Sites",B.x)
B.blt=new A.aP("[[Sites]] lists where your company's wagons are kept. An Admin, a Reliability user and a Viewer hold [[All sites]], including sites added later, or only the sites chosen for them. An Inspector holds only the sites they are given.",B.x)
B.bm1=new A.aP("[[Add site]] creates a site, and [[Rename]] on a row changes its name. A new site reaches everyone with [[All sites]] at once. To give it to an inspector, or to someone with chosen sites, use [[Change role\u2026]] on their row in Users and tick it.",B.cj)
B.Tm=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin, choose a client in the top bar first.",B.co)
B.b2F=s([B.bku,B.ae5,B.a2F,B.aer,B.a31,B.bhY,B.ae1,B.blt,B.bm1,B.Tm],t.f)
B.bb6=s(["dashboard","wagon-page","mgmt-users","mgmt-scopes"],t.s)
B.afY=new A.dG("mgmt-registers","Asset Register","Asset Register lists your wagons and your sites; an admin with [[All sites]] adds and edits them, and everyone else reads them.",B.fa,B.bgv,B.x,B.b2F,B.bb6)
B.bgz=new A.m2("users")
B.bm_=new A.aP("Users answers: who in your company can sign in, with which role, and whose names can be picked on a shared tablet? Your company's Admin with [[All sites]] manages both lists. Everyone else reads them.",B.x)
B.aD8=s(["[[People with a login]]: everyone who signs in with their own email and password. Each row shows the role, the sites ([[All sites]], or the sites chosen for them) and the status: [[Active]], [[Invite pending]] or [[Deactivated]]. [[Show inactive]] adds the deactivated people. A row marked [[Choose sites]] belongs to someone whose sites have not been chosen yet: they keep every site until an admin with [[All sites]] picks.","[[Inspectors]]: the names people pick on a tablet signed in with your company's shared login. Someone with a login is listed here too, tagged [[Login]], and is managed above.","At sign-off, the [[Reliability user]] is chosen from the active names in the [[Reliability]] category and the active people with a login whose role is Admin or Reliability.","To be emailed by [[Notifications]], a name needs an email address. A person with a login always has one."],t.s)
B.a2V=new A.cD(B.aD8,B.x)
B.bkw=new A.aP("Above the list, the [[Choose sites]] filter lists only the people whose sites have not been chosen yet. It is there while there are any.",B.cj)
B.adF=new A.bV("Inviting someone",B.cj)
B.b9B=s(["Press [[Invite person]].","Enter their [[Email]], [[First name]] and [[Last name]].","Choose their [[Role]]. For an Admin, a Reliability user or a Viewer, pick [[All sites]], or [[Choose sites]] and tick at least one site. For an [[Inspector]], tick at least one site.","Press [[Send invite]]."],t.s)
B.buR=new A.kq(B.b9B,B.cj)
B.bkP=new A.aP("[[Invite sent]] means they have an email with a link to set their password. [[Invite created]] means no email went out: press [[Copy link]] and send the link yourself. While the invite is pending, the row shows a [[Resend invite]] button, which emails a fresh link, and its [[Actions]] menu has [[Copy invite link]], which gives you one to send. Someone who has already accepted gets [[Send password reset]] in the same place.",B.cj)
B.aei=new A.bV("Changing or ending access",B.cj)
B.b4V=s(["[[Change role\u2026]] picks a new role or changes their sites. A new role starts with no sites chosen: pick [[All sites]], or [[Choose sites]] and tick at least one.","Taking a site away from someone also stops them finishing an inspection there \u2014 let them sync first.","[[Edit name\u2026]] corrects how their name is shown.","[[Deactivate\u2026]] stops them signing in, on the dashboard or a tablet. Their past inspections and sign-offs are kept. [[Reactivate\u2026]] lets them sign in again with their existing password.","You cannot deactivate yourself, and a change that would leave your company without an admin for [[All sites]] is refused. To hand over, make someone else an Admin for All sites first.","Someone already in your company cannot be invited again: change their role instead."],t.s)
B.a3d=new A.cD(B.b4V,B.cj)
B.adM=new A.bV("Inspectors",B.cj)
B.bm4=new A.aP("[[Add inspector]] adds an inspector by first and last name, with its client and site. [[Edit]] on a row changes it, and the row's [[More]] menu has [[Deactivate user]] and [[Delete name\u2026]]. A deleted name leaves the list for good, but past inspections keep it. A row tagged [[Login]] belongs to someone with a login: manage them in People with a login.",B.cj)
B.blQ=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin, choose a client in the top bar first. You also have [[Delete user\u2026]], which removes a login for good once you type the person's email.",B.co)
B.bdZ=s([B.bm_,B.a2V,B.bkw,B.adF,B.buR,B.bkP,B.aei,B.a3d,B.adM,B.bm4,B.blQ],t.f)
B.bce=s(["start-roles","start-signin","mgmt-registers","mgmt-support"],t.s)
B.afP=new A.dG("mgmt-users","Users","Users lists the people in your company who have a login and the names picked on the shared tablet; an admin with [[All sites]] invites people and sets their role and sites.",B.fa,B.bgz,B.x,B.bdZ,B.bce)
B.bgr=new A.m2("devices")
B.bkj=new A.aP("Inspection devices answers: which tablets can sign in to your company's data, at which site, and when did each last sync? Only your company's Admin with [[All sites]] sees this tab. A tablet signs in with a one-time code instead of a person's email.",B.x)
B.b_D=s(["Each row shows the device [[Name]], its [[Site]] ([[All sites]] or one site), its status and [[Last synced]] ([[Never]] until it has synced).","[[Waiting for pairing]]: a code was issued and the tablet has not used it yet. [[Active]]: the tablet is paired. [[Disabled]]: the tablet can no longer sign in."],t.s)
B.a3k=new A.cD(B.b_D,B.x)
B.aee=new A.bV("Adding a tablet",B.x)
B.aTG=s(["Press [[Add device]].","Enter a [[Device name]] and choose its [[Site]], or [[All sites]].","Press [[Add device]] again. The code appears with a QR code for Wagon Inspector on Google Play.","On the tablet, scan the QR code to install the app, choose Enter device code and type the code."],t.s)
B.buP=new A.kq(B.aTG,B.x)
B.bkJ=new A.aP("A code works once and expires after seven days. It is shown only while its window is open: write it down or type it in before you press [[Done]]. If it is lost, press [[New code]].",B.x)
B.adR=new A.bV("Looking after a device",B.x)
B.bdy=s(["[[New code]] issues a fresh code, for a code that expired unused or a tablet that signed itself out. A tablet that is already paired stays signed in.","A tablet lost or stolen, or a code used by a tablet you do not recognise? Do not use [[New code]]: the missing tablet would stay signed in. Press [[Disable]] (it deletes its data when it next connects), then [[Enable]] to get a code for the replacement. Waiting an hour between the two makes sure it is cut off first.","[[Rename]] changes the name shown here.","[[Disable]] signs the tablet out and deletes its local data the next time it connects. Anything not yet synced on it is lost.","[[Enable]] lets a disabled device back in and issues a new code. A device that WQMS disabled can be enabled by WQMS only. A tablet that was offline throughout and comes back within the hour can keep syncing until its sign-in refreshes (up to an hour), then signs out and needs the new code."],t.s)
B.a2K=new A.cD(B.bdy,B.x)
B.b3v=s([B.bkj,B.a3k,B.aee,B.buP,B.bkJ,B.adR,B.a2K,B.Tm],t.f)
B.b3c=s(["mgmt-users","start-roles","start-signin"],t.s)
B.ag6=new A.dG("mgmt-devices","Inspection devices","Inspection devices lists the tablets that sign in with a one-time code; an admin with [[All sites]] adds them and issues new codes.",B.fa,B.bgr,B.x,B.b3v,B.b3c)
B.bgy=new A.m2("thresholds")
B.blv=new A.aP("Thresholds answers: what severity should a crack be, and which cracks are graded too low? It has two views, [[Severity matrix]] and [[Specific thresholds]]; the tab opens on the matrix.",B.x)
B.aef=new A.bV("The severity matrix",B.x)
B.bl3=new A.aP("A severity matrix belongs to one company and one asset type, such as QHCH Master, and is laid out like the Main Frame table: a row for Vital and for Structural cracks at each depth, Full, Partial and Shallow, and a column for each severity, Minor, Severe and Critical. When an inspector captures a crack, the matrix suggests its severity from the crack's location type, depth and length. The inspector can change it; choosing a lower severity needs a reason.",B.x)
B.b99=s(["Each row has three boxes, one for Minor, Severe and Critical, and each box has a dropdown beside it: a length, [[All]] or [[N/A]]. [[All]] means every length is that severity, and the other two become N/A. [[N/A]] means that severity does not apply to the row.","With a length in each box, you type two numbers in millimetres. Minor reads **< a**: you type a. Severe runs from a to b: a is filled in for you, and you type b. Critical is anything longer than b, and is filled in for you. So a crack of exactly a is Severe, a crack of exactly b is Severe, and a crack just over b is Critical.","If Minor is [[All]] or [[N/A]], Severe's first number is no longer filled in: you type it, or leave it blank to start from 0. If Severe is [[N/A]], Critical starts at a and reads **\u2265 a**, so a crack of exactly a is not left ungraded. If Critical is [[N/A]], you can leave b blank and Severe reads **\u2265 a**.","The length is the max length for L, T, I and M cracks and the total length for X.","Each row is checked as you type, and a message under a box says what to fix before the matrix can be saved. A length no box covers is only a warning: a crack of that length gets no suggestion and is graded by hand.","A row saved before this input existed and written in a form it cannot show reads **This row was entered in the old format**. The row is read-only; press [[Reset row]] to clear that row and enter it again. Other rows are not affected.","Non-structural cracks are never in the matrix. Its last row shows the guidance for them, Cracked, Broken and Loss of function, and they are graded by hand when the crack is captured."],t.s)
B.a32=new A.cD(B.b99,B.x)
B.b3A=s(["Choose the [[Asset type]]. A type that has no matrix yet says **no matrix**; press [[Create matrix]] to start one.","In each row, enter the lengths, or choose [[All]] or [[N/A]] in a box's dropdown.","Press [[Save matrix]]. [[Discard changes]] puts the saved values back."],t.s)
B.buT=new A.kq(B.b3A,B.cj)
B.bl0=new A.aP("[[Clone to\u2026]] copies the matrix to another asset type of the same company, such as QHCH Slave; if that type already has a matrix, its values are replaced. [[Delete matrix]] removes it: cracks on that asset type then get no suggested severity from a matrix. Specific thresholds are not affected.",B.cj)
B.aem=new A.bV("How a specific threshold works",B.x)
B.bla=new A.aP("A specific threshold sets the severity of a crack at one location, ahead of the matrix there. It is for a part that needs limits of its own: for example, every L or T crack of Full depth at the Drawbar End that is 200 mm or longer is Severe. Where no specific threshold matches a crack, the matrix suggests its severity.",B.x)
B.bbV=s(["A specific threshold has a scope, the cracks it covers and a length. The scope is an asset type and, if you choose them, a location (a zone, a region or a single view) and a location type, Vital or Structural. With no location it covers the whole asset type. Non-structural cracks cannot have one: they are graded by hand.","The cracks are the [[Crack types]] and the [[Depth]] classes you select, more than one of each if you like. Select none to cover every crack type, or every depth.","The [[Length (mm)]] is written like a cell of the matrix, such as \u2265200, 100-200 or all. It is the max length for L, T, I and M cracks and the total length for X. The [[Severity]] is what the threshold assigns to a crack that matches.","When more than one specific threshold matches a crack, the one at the more exact location wins (a view, then a region, a zone, a component, then the whole asset type); at the same location, the more severe one wins. A threshold that does not match a crack leaves it to the next one, and then to the matrix.","A threshold belongs to one company and is checked only against that company's wagons. One that is not [[Active]] is ignored.","A threshold saved for a whole model, with no component, applies to every component of it and overrides each one's matrix. The list reads **All components of** the model for it, and the form warns before it is saved."],t.s)
B.a3j=new A.cD(B.bbV,B.x)
B.adP=new A.bV("Rules in the old format",B.x)
B.bkQ=new A.aP("Rules written before this release, a measure and a trigger value, stay in the list marked **Old format \u2014 not used**. They no longer suggest a severity or raise an alert. Click one to enter it again: its crack type and length are filled in where they can be, and the dialog says what is missing, such as an owner company, an asset type or a severity. A rule that was on Non-structural cracks is saved only once you choose Vital or Structural for it; otherwise delete it. Enter a length and press [[Save]] to turn it into a specific threshold. A threshold whose notes say it was converted from an old rule is already one: check it, then switch it to [[Active]].",B.x)
B.aeh=new A.bV("Where an alert shows",B.x)
B.b6o=s(["On the defect's page, as [[Below suggested severity]]."],t.s)
B.a38=new A.cD(B.b6o,B.x)
B.b97=s(["Alerts come from the severity matrix and from active specific thresholds.","Saving or changing a matrix checks every open defect again, older ones included, so the first matrix saved may mark defects that were already graded below it.","A defect the inspector graded lower on purpose, with a reason, shows that reason on its page. The reason counts only while the severity it was lowered from is still the one suggested: if the matrix or a threshold now suggests a higher one, the defect is marked without it."],t.s)
B.a33=new A.cD(B.b97,B.x)
B.bi6=new A.ho("A threshold suggests a severity and flags a defect graded below it. It does not change the defect's severity and it does not send email.",B.x)
B.adU=new A.bV("Who can change thresholds",B.x)
B.bkT=new A.aP("Everyone reads the matrix and the list, and a click on a rule opens it. A matrix or a rule is added, edited or deleted by an Admin with [[All sites]] of the company that owns it, or by its Manager or Coordinator where a company still has those older roles, and by a WQMS admin. An Admin with chosen sites, a Reliability user or a Viewer cannot change one.",B.x)
B.aDa=s(["Open [[Specific thresholds]] and press [[Add specific threshold]].","Under [[Scope]], choose the [[Asset type]]. To limit the threshold to one place, choose a [[Location]] and, if you like, a [[Location type]].","Under [[Crack]], select the [[Crack types]] and [[Depth]] classes it covers, or select none for all.","Under [[Rule]], enter the [[Length (mm)]] and choose the [[Severity]].","Press [[Add]]. The threshold's name is made from these choices."],t.s)
B.buQ=new A.kq(B.aDa,B.cj)
B.blU=new A.aP("Click a rule to edit it. [[Delete]] on its row removes it, and it stops setting a severity at once.",B.cj)
B.bly=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin, choose a client in the top bar first. A rule flagged [[No owner: not alerting]] belongs to no company, so it applies to no wagon: open it and choose an [[Owner company]].",B.co)
B.bcm=s([B.blv,B.aef,B.bl3,B.a32,B.buT,B.bl0,B.aem,B.bla,B.a3j,B.adP,B.bkQ,B.aeh,B.a38,B.a33,B.bi6,B.adU,B.bkT,B.buQ,B.blU,B.bly],t.f)
B.b50=s(["dashboard","defect-page","mgmt-scopes"],t.s)
B.ag_=new A.dG("mgmt-thresholds","Thresholds","Thresholds holds the severity matrix and the specific thresholds for your wagons; together they suggest a crack's severity, and an alert is raised when a defect is graded below it.",B.fa,B.bgy,B.x,B.bcm,B.b50)
B.bgt=new A.m2("notifications")
B.bkK=new A.aP("Notifications answers: who gets an email when an inspection is published, for which wagon models, and when? Each row is one person. [[Assets]] says which models the row covers and [[When]] says when the email goes. Everyone reads the list. It is changed by an Admin with [[All sites]] of the company that owns the wagons, or by its Manager or Coordinator where a company still has those older roles, and by a WQMS admin. An Admin with chosen sites, a Reliability user or a Viewer cannot change it.",B.x)
B.adz=new A.bV("Who can be chosen",B.x)
B.bcM=s(["People on your [[Users]] list who have no login of their own, and people who do have a login, a Viewer included. A person with a login reads **Name (login)**.","People of other companies that work at your sites, such as a contractor. Their company is shown after their name.","Each person has one row. Someone who already has a row is not offered again: edit their row instead."],t.s)
B.a2W=new A.cD(B.bcM,B.x)
B.aeo=new A.bV("When an email is sent",B.x)
B.bdT=s(["[[Automatic]]: sent when an inspection is published and it records a new defect, a defect that has grown, or one now at a higher severity, at or above the level in [[Send for]]: [[Minor or higher]], [[Severe or higher]] or [[Critical]]. The email lists the defects at or above that level.","[[Optional]]: the inspector chooses whether to send it when publishing, and can add a comment. The publish dialog lists these people under [[Also notify (optional):]], unticked. The email lists every new, grown or higher-severity defect.","[[Assets]] is [[All]], every model including ones added later, or [[Choose models]] with the models you tick."],t.s)
B.a2J=new A.cD(B.bdT,B.x)
B.bhV=new A.ho("The rows are read when an inspection is published. A person added afterwards is not emailed about inspections that were published before.",B.x)
B.bi2=new A.ho("A person whose login is limited to chosen sites is only emailed about wagons at those sites. The tablet's publish list may still name them for a wagon elsewhere; they are not emailed about it.",B.x)
B.adx=new A.bV("A person with no email address",B.x)
B.blo=new A.aP("A name on the Users list with no email address is flagged [[No email]]: nothing can be sent to them until one is entered. A person with a login always has an address, so is never flagged. [[Add email]] saves the address on their row in Users, so it shows there too, and the flag goes. It is shown only to someone who may edit the Users list of that person's company, which is a WQMS admin or that company's Admin with [[All sites]]. For anyone else the flag says to ask an administrator of that company.",B.x)
B.blu=new A.aP("[[Inactive \u2014 not sent]] marks a person who has been switched off, or who no longer works at your sites. They get nothing until that changes.",B.x)
B.ae3=new A.bV("Adding and changing rows",B.cj)
B.bcG=s(["Press [[Add person]].","Choose the [[Person]]. If they have no address yet, [[Add email]] under the field enters one.","Under [[Assets]], keep [[All]], or choose [[Choose models]] and tick the models.","Under [[When]], choose [[Automatic]] and a level in [[Send for]], or [[Optional]].","Press [[Save]]."],t.s)
B.buO=new A.kq(B.bcG,B.cj)
B.bkv=new A.aP("[[Edit]] on a row changes it, and [[Remove]] deletes it: that person stops getting emails at once. Removing a row does not remove the person from Users.",B.cj)
B.Tl=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin, choose a client in the top bar first. With [[All clients]] selected, the tab asks you to pick one.",B.co)
B.b5e=s([B.bkK,B.adz,B.a2W,B.aeo,B.a2J,B.bhV,B.bi2,B.adx,B.blo,B.blu,B.ae3,B.buO,B.bkv,B.Tl],t.f)
B.aP8=s(["mgmt-users","mgmt-thresholds","inspection-page","workspace"],t.s)
B.afQ=new A.dG("mgmt-notifications","Notifications","Notifications lists who is emailed when an inspection is published, for which wagon models and when; an admin with [[All sites]] chooses the people, and everyone else reads the list.",B.fa,B.bgt,B.x,B.b5e,B.aP8)
B.bgw=new A.m2("scopes")
B.bl8=new A.aP("Scopes answers: what does each kind of inspection cover? A scope is a named set of views of one model and component. The scope chosen when an inspection is created sets which views it covers.",B.x)
B.aX6=s(["Scopes are grouped by model and component. Each row shows the [[Name]], how many of the views it covers ([[Whole model]] when it covers them all), whether it applies to [[All units]] or to chosen ones, and its status: [[Active]] or [[Retired]].","[[Retired scopes]] are in a group of their own at the bottom, closed until you click it.","Click a scope to see its views."],t.s)
B.a2M=new A.cD(B.aX6,B.x)
B.ae8=new A.bV("How a scope is used",B.x)
B.b9y=s(["A scope belongs to the company that owns the wagons, not to whoever inspects them.","When an inspection is created it is offered the active scopes that apply to its wagon, and [[Custom]]. Custom is not a stored scope: the views are picked for that one inspection.","Changing a scope affects new inspections only. An inspection keeps the views it was created with."],t.s)
B.a3c=new A.cD(B.b9y,B.x)
B.aea=new A.bV("Who can change scopes",B.x)
B.blI=new A.aP("Everyone reads the list. A scope is added, edited, retired or restored by an Admin with [[All sites]] of the company that owns it, or by its Manager or Coordinator where a company still has those older roles, and by a WQMS admin. An Admin with chosen sites, a Reliability user or a Viewer cannot change one.",B.x)
B.bdD=s(["Press [[Add scope]] and give it a [[Name]].","Under [[Target]], choose [[Whole model]] for every wagon of a [[Model]] and [[Component]], or [[Specific units]] to tick the wagons.","Under [[Views]], tick the views the scope covers.","Press [[Add]]."],t.s)
B.buU=new A.kq(B.bdD,B.cj)
B.blE=new A.aP("[[Retire]] takes a scope out of the choices for new inspections without deleting it, and [[Restore]] brings it back. A retired scope has to be restored before it can be edited.",B.cj)
B.bcN=s([B.bl8,B.FW,B.a2M,B.ae8,B.a3c,B.aea,B.blI,B.buU,B.blE,B.Tl],t.f)
B.aTH=s(["inspections","workspace","mgmt-registers","mgmt-thresholds"],t.s)
B.afT=new A.dG("mgmt-scopes","Scopes","Scopes lists the inspection scopes of the company that owns the wagons; each scope sets which views an inspection covers.",B.fa,B.bgw,B.x,B.bcN,B.aTH)
B.bgx=new A.m2("support")
B.bkB=new A.aP("User Support is how you reach the WQMS team from inside the dashboard, when something is wrong, unclear or missing. Everyone who can sign in has it, a View only account included.",B.x)
B.aej=new A.bV("Sending a request",B.x)
B.beN=s(["Under [[File a request]], choose the [[Type]]: [[Report a bug]], [[Ask for help]] or [[Request a feature]].","In [[Message]], write what happened and what you expected to happen.","Press [[Send]]. The page answers [[Sent \u2014 an administrator will reply here.]]"],t.s)
B.buW=new A.kq(B.beN,B.x)
B.ae_=new A.bV("Reading the reply",B.x)
B.bkZ=new A.aP("[[MY REQUESTS]] lists what you have sent, each with its status: [[Open]] or [[Addressed]]. Once the WQMS team has dealt with a request, their reply is under [[ADMIN RESPONSE]].",B.x)
B.bi7=new A.ho("An addressed request cannot be reopened. If more is needed, send a new one.",B.x)
B.adE=new A.bV("The inbox",B.co)
B.blf=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you also have [[Inbox]]: every request users have sent, from the dashboard and from the tablet app, filtered with [[Open]] and [[Addressed]]. Open a request, write what you did in [[Admin notes (optional)]] and press [[Mark addressed]]. The requester sees your notes. Marking a request addressed stamps your name and the time, and cannot be undone.",B.co)
B.b7H=s([B.bkB,B.aej,B.buW,B.ae_,B.bkZ,B.bi7,B.adE,B.blf],t.f)
B.b9U=s(["start-roles","start-signin"],t.s)
B.ag1=new A.dG("mgmt-support","User Support","User Support is where you report a bug, ask for help or request a feature, and read the replies to the requests you have sent.",B.fa,B.bgx,B.x,B.b7H,B.b9U)
B.bgq=new A.m2("clients")
B.bkM=new A.aP("Clients lists the client companies, each with its logo and how many sites and people it has. The [[Admins (All sites)]] column counts only the admins for [[All sites]]: an Admin with chosen sites cannot manage the client's people, sites and wagons.",B.x)
B.bdu=s(["[[Add client]] creates a company: its name, an optional first site and an optional logo. Without a first site the client gets a default site named after it, so that a wagon always has a site.","Click a client for its sites and its people. While it has no admin for [[All sites]], [[Invite first admin]] invites one: pick [[All sites]] for them, and that admin then manages the client's own people, sites and wagons.","[[All clients]] returns to the list."],t.s)
B.a3r=new A.cD(B.bdu,B.x)
B.bl9=new A.aP("On a client's page, [[People with a login]] and [[Sites]] are the same lists as in Users and in Asset Register, for that client alone. You can invite people, change their roles, and add or rename sites there without switching to that client in the top bar. Its [[Inspectors]], the names for its shared tablet, are not on this page: they are in [[Users]], with that client chosen in the top bar.",B.x)
B.bi0=new A.ho("When you add a client, its page opens straight away. If the logo could not be saved, the message says so, and you can upload it in [[Client logos]].",B.x)
B.b6g=s([B.bkM,B.a3r,B.bl9,B.bi0],t.f)
B.b4p=s(["mgmt-users","mgmt-registers","mgmt-logos"],t.s)
B.afN=new A.dG("mgmt-clients","Clients","Clients lists the client companies and is where you add a new one, with its sites and its first admin.",B.fa,B.bgq,B.co,B.b6g,B.b4p)
B.bgu=new A.m2("reference")
B.blj=new A.aP("Reference data is where each wagon model's components, zones, regions and views are maintained, with the reference image of each view. It opens on one model's views; open a view to work on it.",B.x)
B.bbA=s(["[[Locator maps]] is a page of its own, for the maps that show where a zone or a region sits.","A retired view cannot be picked for new inspections and is removed from any saved scope that lists it. Defects recorded on it keep their history. [[Show retired]] lists what has been retired.","Leaving the tab with unsaved changes asks before it discards them."],t.s)
B.a2G=new A.cD(B.bbA,B.x)
B.ack=new A.Hj(B.co)
B.aX3=s([B.blj,B.a2G,B.ack],t.f)
B.b3R=s(["mgmt-scopes","mgmt-logos"],t.s)
B.ag0=new A.dG("mgmt-reference","Reference data","Reference data is where you maintain each wagon model's components, zones, regions and views, with their images and locator maps.",B.fa,B.bgu,B.co,B.aX3,B.b3R)
B.bgs=new A.m2("logos")
B.blF=new A.aP("Client logos gives each client company its logo. The dashboard shows the logo of the company that owns the wagons on screen at the far left of the top bar.",B.x)
B.bcc=s(["There is one row per company, with the logo it has now or [[No logo]].","[[Upload logo\u2026]] adds a logo and [[Replace logo\u2026]] changes it. The file has to be a JPEG or a PNG.","There is no delete: a logo is only ever replaced."],t.s)
B.a2Z=new A.cD(B.bcc,B.x)
B.bi3=new A.ho("A logo has to be at least 128 px on its longer side and no larger than 25 MB. One over 1024 px is scaled down to that, and a PNG keeps its transparency. A file that is refused changes nothing: the reason shows under that company's row. A new client's logo can also be chosen when the client is added, in [[Clients]].",B.x)
B.b2S=s([B.blF,B.a2Z,B.bi3],t.f)
B.b9D=s(["mgmt-clients","mgmt-reference"],t.s)
B.afU=new A.dG("mgmt-logos","Client logos","Client logos is where you upload each client's logo, which the dashboard shows at the left of the top bar.",B.fa,B.bgs,B.co,B.b2S,B.b9D)
B.b5o=s([B.afV,B.afZ,B.afR,B.ag8,B.afS,B.afM,B.afW,B.ag2,B.ag7,B.afO,B.afX,B.ag5,B.ag4,B.ag3,B.afY,B.afP,B.ag6,B.ag_,B.afQ,B.afT,B.ag1,B.afN,B.ag0,B.afU],t.iO)
B.bkG=new A.aP("If the top bar shows [[View only]], your account can look but not change anything: it holds no role that changes records, so the buttons that add, edit or delete are left out. You can still read every page, export an inspection's report, change your own details in [[My profile]] and send a request from [[User Support]]. To change records, ask your company's admin for a different role: [[Users]] in Management shows who that is. If [[View only]] is not shown and one button is still missing, your role does not include it.",B.x)
B.b36=s([B.bkG],t.f)
B.af_=new A.d2("faq-view-only","Why can't I change anything?",B.b36,"Every page",B.x,"start-roles")
B.bke=new A.aP("The model filter follows you: a model chosen on one fleet page stays chosen on the others, so that the pages never disagree about which wagons they count. While it is set, a pill with the model's name sits beside the page title. Its \u2715 ([[Show all models]]) clears the filter, and so do [[Reset filters]] and the [[All models]] chip.",B.x)
B.b5q=s([B.bke],t.f)
B.af0=new A.d2("faq-model-filter","Why does every page still show only one model, and how do I clear it?",B.b5q,"Every page",B.x,"start-navigation")
B.bl7=new A.aP("It is the logo of the company that owns the wagons on screen, not of the company you work for. It appears once that company has a logo, and until then the space is empty.",B.x)
B.bld=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you have the client switcher in that place instead. You upload each client's logo in Management, [[Client logos]].",B.co)
B.bct=s([B.bl7,B.bld],t.f)
B.aev=new A.d2("faq-logo","Where does the logo at the top left come from?",B.bct,"Every page",B.x,"start-navigation")
B.blK=new A.aP("Because decommissioned wagons are left out of it. The total under [[Inspected]] is your in-service plus parked wagons, and the percentage is the share of those with at least one inspection. The wagon count in the top bar is the whole register, decommissioned wagons included. With a model chosen, the card also counts that model only.",B.x)
B.bdn=s([B.blK],t.f)
B.aeF=new A.d2("faq-inspected-total","Why is the total on the Inspected card smaller than the number of wagons in the register?",B.bdn,"Dashboard",B.x,"dashboard")
B.blP=new A.aP("Any wagon with at least one current defect. A current defect is one that is not repaired and was not found clear at a later inspection. That includes a missed defect while it still carries the severity it was last seen with. Decommissioned wagons are not counted.",B.x)
B.bbR=s([B.blP],t.f)
B.aeE=new A.d2("faq-wagons-with-defects","What counts as a wagon with defects?",B.bbR,"Dashboard",B.x,"dashboard")
B.bkD=new A.aP("The two rows count different things: the first counts wagons and the second counts defects. [[Wagons with areas not inspected]] is the wagons with a missed defect, a missed area, or a location marked not inspected at their latest inspection. [[Missed defects]] is the missed defects that still carry a severity, which are the ones also counted in Current Defects.",B.x)
B.b3V=s([B.bkD],t.f)
B.aeW=new A.d2("faq-not-inspected-vs-missed","What does Not Inspected count, and why is Missed defects a different number?",B.b3V,"Dashboard",B.x,"dashboard")
B.blZ=new A.aP("It includes repairs recorded with a stabilising action, but not defects whose status is still Stabilised. On the [[Repaired or Stabilised]] card and on the Repaired page, [[Repaired]] is a full repair and [[Stabilised]] is a repair recorded with a stabilising action, such as a crack arrest. A defect whose status is still Stabilised is held but still there, so it is a current defect and is counted on the [[Current Defects]] card.",B.x)
B.bbi=s([B.blZ],t.f)
B.aeA=new A.d2("faq-repaired-stabilised","Does Repaired include stabilised defects?",B.bbi,"Dashboard",B.x,"repairs")
B.bln=new A.aP("[[Unknown model]] holds the defects recorded against a unit that is not in the wagon register. Once the wagon is added in Management, [[Asset Register]], its defects are filed under its model.",B.x)
B.b3G=s([B.bln],t.f)
B.aeG=new A.d2("faq-unknown-model","What does Unknown model mean?",B.b3G,"Dashboard",B.x,"dashboard")
B.blV=new A.aP("Yes. The three boxes on [[Wagon Fleet]] count only the wagons of the model you have chosen, and each opens the Asset Register on that status and that model. The line under [[In-service]] and [[Parked]] gives the fleet total they are part of, which leaves decommissioned wagons out.",B.x)
B.bd7=s([B.blV],t.f)
B.aey=new A.d2("faq-status-boxes-model","Do the In-service, Parked and Decommissioned boxes follow the model filter?",B.bd7,"Dashboard",B.x,"dashboard")
B.bkC=new A.aP("No, if the update was made in a later inspection. An inspection's page and its report show each defect with the status and severity that inspection recorded, not its latest ones. The exception is repair work recorded outside an inspection: it is added to the defect's latest inspection, published or not, and that inspection's page and report then show the repair.",B.x)
B.be5=s([B.bkC],t.f)
B.aeY=new A.d2("faq-published-unchanged","I updated a crack later. Did the earlier published inspection change?",B.be5,"Inspections",B.x,"inspection-page")
B.blq=new A.aP("They count what that inspection recorded, each finding once. [[Defects]] counts cracks and access-structure findings, and [[Damage]] counts damage. A finding the inspection could not inspect is counted under [[Not inspected]] instead, together with the locations it marked not inspected. One it repaired is counted under [[Repaired]].",B.x)
B.aTL=s([B.blq],t.f)
B.aeL=new A.d2("faq-summary-counts","What do the four counts on an inspection count?",B.aTL,"Inspections",B.x,"inspection-page")
B.bkI=new A.aP("No. A repaired defect is not carried to the next inspection and it leaves Current Defects, but its record stays. It is listed on the [[Repaired]] page, and its own page keeps the full [[History]].",B.x)
B.b2P=s([B.bkI],t.f)
B.aex=new A.d2("faq-repaired-not-carried","A repaired defect is no longer listed at the next inspection. Is it lost?",B.b2P,"Inspections",B.x,"repairs")
B.bkR=new A.aP("Not from the dashboard: it has no button that deletes an inspection. An inspection can be deleted in the Wagon Inspector tablet app until it is published, and it then leaves the dashboard too. A published inspection cannot be deleted.",B.x)
B.b8x=s([B.bkR],t.f)
B.aeV=new A.d2("faq-delete-inspection","Can I delete an inspection?",B.b8x,"Inspections",B.d2,null)
B.blp=new A.aP("The workspace opens only while an inspection is [[In progress]], so [[Open workspace]] is offered at that status alone. On a [[Draft]], press [[Start inspection]] on its page first. A [[Scope complete]] or [[Inspection complete]] inspection has [[Reopen]], which returns it to In progress and clears its completion until it is completed again. A [[Published]] inspection can be reopened only by a WQMS admin.",B.x)
B.b4I=s([B.blp],t.f)
B.aeT=new A.d2("faq-workspace-locked","Why can't I open the workspace for this inspection?",B.b4I,"Inspections",B.d2,"inspection-page")
B.blc=new A.aP("The view, or every view under that zone or region, is outside the scope the inspection was created with. The tile is dimmed and tagged **Not in scope** with the scope's name. It still opens.",B.x)
B.baZ=s([B.blc],t.f)
B.af2=new A.d2("faq-not-in-scope","What does Not in scope on a Capture tile mean?",B.baZ,"Inspections",B.d2,"workspace")
B.bks=new A.aP("Because [[Prior]] and [[Missed]] are not limited by the scope. A defect carried from an earlier inspection is listed wherever it sits on the wagon, and each one has to be updated before [[Confirm scope complete]] is offered.",B.x)
B.b5t=s([B.bks],t.f)
B.aeQ=new A.d2("faq-scope-priors","Why do defects outside this inspection's scope still appear and block completion?",B.b5t,"Inspections",B.d2,"workspace")
B.bkr=new A.aP("A missed defect stays on the list because the crack is still on the wagon. It could not be re-inspected, so it keeps the severity it was last seen with and its [[Status]] reads [[Missed]]. Repaired defects are no longer current, so they are on the [[Repaired]] page instead.",B.x)
B.bdp=s([B.bkr],t.f)
B.aeu=new A.d2("faq-current-missed","Why does Current Defects include missed cracks, and where are the repaired ones?",B.bdp,"Current Defects",B.x,"defects")
B.bkg=new A.aP("[[Data]] is the defect's code: one short code made from what was recorded. For a crack it is built from the location type, the length, the crack type, the depth and the thickness; a damage reads D- and its damage type, for example D-Wear.",B.x)
B.b6a=s([B.bkg],t.f)
B.aeH=new A.d2("faq-crack-data","What is in the Data column?",B.b6a,"Current Defects",B.x,"defects")
B.bkL=new A.aP("A [[Custom ID]] is your own identifier for an area of a reference view, so that a defect here can be matched to your own crack records. Every defect whose pin sits inside the area shows that ID in the [[Custom ID]] column, after [[Data]], and on the defect's page under the photos. The ID follows the area, not the defect: change the area or its ID and it changes on those defects too. The column only appears when at least one defect in the list has an ID. Lists that show a defect's [[Data]] code without columns, such as the repaired defects, the lists you open from a chart or a count, an inspection's summary and the list beside the Hot Spots map, show the ID right after the code, separated by a dot; a defect with no ID shows nothing extra. The WQMS team sets the areas and their IDs; you can reach them from [[User Support]] in Management.",B.x)
B.bls=new A.aP("You set a Custom ID in Management \u203a [[Reference data]]: open a view, choose [[Layers]], then [[Custom ID]], draw the area and type the ID.",B.co)
B.bda=s([B.bkL,B.bls],t.f)
B.aeX=new A.d2("faq-custom-id","What is a Custom ID?",B.bda,"Current Defects",B.x,"defects")
B.bm3=new A.aP("A WQMS admin records it, on the defect's page. You can reach the WQMS team from [[User Support]] in Management. Repair work done during an inspection is recorded there, when the defect is updated as [[Repaired]] or [[Stabilised]].",B.x)
B.blY=new A.aP("As a WQMS admin you have [[Mark repaired\u2026]] and [[Mark stabilised\u2026]] on a defect's page, but a repaired defect offers neither and a stabilised one only [[Mark repaired\u2026]]. Neither is offered on a defect opened from a published inspection: open it from [[Current Defects]] instead.",B.co)
B.bea=s([B.bm3,B.blY],t.f)
B.aeS=new A.d2("faq-mark-repaired","Who records repair work that was done outside an inspection?",B.bea,"A defect's page",B.x,"defect-page")
B.bko=new A.aP("Open the defect: when its status is [[Grown]], the page shows **Growth since last inspection**, with the change in millimetres and the lengths before and after. The line needs a length on both that observation and the one before it, so it is absent when either was recorded without one.",B.x)
B.b5U=s([B.bko],t.f)
B.af1=new A.d2("faq-crack-growth","How do I see how much a crack has grown?",B.b5U,"A defect's page",B.x,"defect-page")
B.blJ=new A.aP("[[This inspection]] marks the rows recorded by the inspection you opened the defect from. To open the inspection behind any row of [[History]], click the row to expand it and press [[Open inspection]].",B.x)
B.aJa=s([B.blJ],t.f)
B.aez=new A.d2("faq-this-inspection","What does This inspection mean in a defect's History, and how do I open the inspection?",B.aJa,"A defect's page",B.x,"defect-page")
B.bkn=new A.aP("A tile counts what is marked on that view's crack map, and the Dashboard counts severity. [[Active]] on a tile includes every missed defect, while the Dashboard counts a missed defect only while it still carries a severity. [[Repaired]] on a tile also includes prior repairs marked on the view.",B.x)
B.bel=s([B.bkn],t.f)
B.aeR=new A.d2("faq-hotspot-differs","Why does a Hot Spots tile show a different number from the Dashboard?",B.bel,"Hot Spots",B.x,"hotspots")
B.blO=new A.aP("Press **Show all \u2026 locations** under the tiles. The page shows the ten highest first, and the button appears when there are more. [[Show top 10]] folds the rest away again.",B.x)
B.baV=s([B.blO],t.f)
B.aeI=new A.d2("faq-hotspot-top-ten","How do I see more than the top ten hot spots?",B.baV,"Hot Spots",B.x,"hotspots")
B.bkO=new A.aP("[[Most Severe]] is the wagon's worst current defect, shown as its severity and that defect's status. The counts beside the title describe the fleet under the model filter, not the rows on screen: every wagon that is not decommissioned, the wagons **with defects**, and the wagons **not fully inspected**.",B.x)
B.b7s=s([B.bkO],t.f)
B.aeN=new A.d2("faq-most-severe","What do Most Severe and the counts beside the title mean?",B.b7s,"Wagon Health",B.x,"health")
B.bkl=new A.aP("A wagon's status is changed in one place only: Management, [[Asset Register]], with [[Change status]] on the wagon's row. Wagon Health and a wagon's page are for reading, so that a stray click there cannot take a wagon out of the fleet. [[Change status]] is there for your company's Admin with [[All sites]], for its Manager or Coordinator where a company still has those older roles, and for WQMS admins. Everyone else reads the register.",B.x)
B.ak6=s([B.bkl],t.f)
B.aeO=new A.d2("faq-status-from-health","Why can't I change a wagon's status from Wagon Health?",B.ak6,"Wagon Health",B.d2,"health")
B.bkV=new A.aP("No, not at the same site. Each wagon in the register has one model and one component, so a Master and a Slave are two wagons. Two wagons at one site cannot share a unit number.",B.x)
B.b8M=s([B.bkV],t.f)
B.aet=new A.d2("faq-unit-number","Do a Master and a Slave share a unit number?",B.b8M,"Asset Register",B.x,"mgmt-registers")
B.bkW=new A.aP("The component locks once the wagon has an inspection or is listed in a scope. An inspection keeps the views it was made on, and those belong to the component the wagon had then, so changing it would leave the inspection pointing at another component's views. A wagon locked only by a scope unlocks when you take it out of that scope.",B.x)
B.b5j=s([B.bkW],t.f)
B.aeB=new A.d2("faq-component-locked","Why is a wagon's Component greyed out when I edit it?",B.b5j,"Asset Register",B.cj,"mgmt-registers")
B.bkh=new A.aP("Use [[Import CSV]] on the Wagons list: choose a file, and the preview marks each row [[Add]], [[Skip]] or [[Error]] before anything is written. [[Skip]] is a wagon already in the register. [[Error]] gives its reason beside the row, such as a model that is not an active wagon type, a missing or wrong component, a status that is not one of the three, or a unit number that is in the file twice. [[Commit]] adds the rows marked [[Add]] only, so correct the others in the file and import it again.",B.x)
B.bdc=s([B.bkh],t.f)
B.aeZ=new A.d2("faq-import-wagons","How do I add many wagons at once, and why are some rows marked Error?",B.bdc,"Asset Register",B.cj,"mgmt-registers")
B.bkk=new A.aP("A login that is only an inspector's is for the Wagon Inspector tablet app, so the dashboard refuses it. The dashboard needs another role: Admin, Reliability or Viewer. Ask your company's admin to give you one.",B.x)
B.b3Q=s([B.bkk],t.f)
B.aeU=new A.d2("faq-tablet-login","Why can't I sign in here with the tablet login?",B.b3Q,"Users and signing in",B.x,"start-signin")
B.bkY=new A.aP("Ask for a new one: a page that says the link has expired or was already used needs a fresh link. For an invite, ask your company's admin to resend it. For a password reset, press [[Forgot password?]] on the sign-in page again.",B.x)
B.bdm=s([B.bkY],t.f)
B.aeD=new A.d2("faq-link-expired","My invite or reset link stopped working. What now?",B.bdm,"Users and signing in",B.x,"start-signin")
B.bkU=new A.aP("Send them the link yourself. In [[Users]], open the [[Actions]] menu on their row while the invite is pending: [[Copy invite link]] gives you a link to send, and [[Resend invite]] emails a fresh one. If inviting them ended on [[Invite created]] rather than [[Invite sent]], no email went out at all, and [[Copy link]] there gives you the link.",B.x)
B.b8J=s([B.bkU],t.f)
B.aeM=new A.d2("faq-invite-no-email","Someone I invited did not get the email. What can I do?",B.b8J,"Users and signing in",B.cj,"mgmt-users")
B.bkE=new A.aP("[[People with a login]] sign in with their own email and password. [[Inspectors]] are inspectors and reliability staff with no login of their own, who pick their name on a tablet signed in with your company's shared login. At sign-off, the [[Reliability user]] is chosen from the active names in the [[Reliability]] category and the active people with a login whose role is Admin or Reliability.",B.x)
B.baq=s([B.bkE],t.f)
B.aeC=new A.d2("faq-users-lists","What is the difference between people with a login and names for the shared tablet, and who can be chosen at sign-off?",B.baq,"Users and signing in",B.x,"mgmt-users")
B.bkz=new A.aP("Nobody has chosen that person's sites yet. Until someone does, they keep every site of your company. An admin with [[All sites]] opens [[Change role\u2026]] on their row and picks [[All sites]] or [[Choose sites]].",B.x)
B.b38=s([B.bkz],t.f)
B.aew=new A.d2("faq-choose-sites","What does Choose sites mean in Users?",B.b38,"Users and signing in",B.x,"mgmt-users")
B.bkX=new A.aP("Your access is limited to the sites chosen for you: you see the wagons, inspections and defects of those sites only. Managing people, sites, wagons, Scopes and Thresholds needs an Admin with [[All sites]]. Ask your company's admin if you need more.",B.x)
B.b6Y=s([B.bkX],t.f)
B.aeJ=new A.d2("faq-some-sites","Why do I see only some of our wagons, or cannot edit Thresholds?",B.b6Y,"Users and signing in",B.x,"start-roles")
B.blk=new A.aP("A specific threshold sets the severity of a crack at one location, ahead of the severity matrix there. It covers the crack types and depth classes you choose, and a band of lengths. A defect graded below the severity the matrix or a specific threshold suggests is marked [[Below suggested severity]] on its page. It does not send email, and it does not change the defect's severity.",B.x)
B.bc9=s([B.blk],t.f)
B.aeK=new A.d2("faq-threshold","What is a specific threshold, and does it send an email?",B.bc9,"Thresholds and Scopes",B.x,"mgmt-thresholds")
B.bm2=new A.aP("A scope belongs to the company that owns the wagons, and it is changed by that company's Admin with [[All sites]], by its Manager or Coordinator where a company still has those older roles, or by a WQMS admin. Everyone else reads the list. [[Custom]] is not a stored scope: it is the choice, when an inspection is created, to pick the views for that one inspection. A retired scope has to be restored before it can be edited.",B.x)
B.baI=s([B.bm2],t.f)
B.aeP=new A.d2("faq-scope-owner","Who owns a scope, what is Custom, and why can't I edit a scope?",B.baI,"Thresholds and Scopes",B.x,"mgmt-scopes")
B.b6N=s([B.af_,B.af0,B.aev,B.aeF,B.aeE,B.aeW,B.aeA,B.aeG,B.aey,B.aeY,B.aeL,B.aex,B.aeV,B.aeT,B.af2,B.aeQ,B.aeu,B.aeH,B.aeX,B.aeS,B.af1,B.aez,B.aeR,B.aeI,B.aeN,B.aeO,B.aet,B.aeB,B.aeZ,B.aeU,B.aeD,B.aeM,B.aeC,B.aew,B.aeJ,B.aeK,B.aeP],t.vW)
B.afD=new A.cq("Model","A type of wagon; the model chips at the top of the fleet pages narrow them to one model.","start-navigation",B.x)
B.af4=new A.cq("Component","One of the parts a model is made of, where it has more than one: a wagon of such a model is registered as one component, and each component has its own zones and views.","mgmt-registers",B.x)
B.afu=new A.cq("Zone","A main part of the wagon, and the first of the three levels that say where a defect is: Zone, Region, View.","dashboard",B.x)
B.afw=new A.cq("Region","A part of a zone, and the middle level of a defect's location; a zone can also have views with no region.","dashboard",B.x)
B.afm=new A.cq("View","One drawing of part of the wagon: a defect is pinned on a view, a scope is a set of views, and a hot spot is a view.","hotspots",B.x)
B.af7=new A.cq("Unit","The unit number that identifies a wagon; the dashboard also uses the word for the wagon itself.","mgmt-registers",B.x)
B.afr=new A.cq("Default site","The site that is created together with a company, so that every wagon has a site.","mgmt-registers",B.x)
B.afn=new A.cq("Locator map","A picture that shows where a zone or a region sits on the wagon, maintained on the [[Locator maps]] page of Reference data.","mgmt-reference",B.co)
B.afF=new A.cq("In-service","The status of a wagon in normal use.","mgmt-registers",B.x)
B.af3=new A.cq("Parked","The status of a wagon that is out of use for now but still in the fleet: it stays in the fleet counts and can still be inspected.","mgmt-registers",B.x)
B.afv=new A.cq("Decommissioned","The status of a wagon taken out of the fleet: its history is kept, it can no longer be inspected, and its defects leave the current counts.","start-overview",B.x)
B.afI=new A.cq("Current defect","A defect that is open now: not repaired, not found clear at a later inspection and, if it was missed, still carrying a severity.","defects",B.x)
B.afb=new A.cq("Severity","How serious a defect is: Critical, Severe or Minor. A damage or an access structure can instead be None: recorded and counted as a current defect, shown in grey, but not graded.","defects",B.x)
B.afE=new A.cq("Defect number","How a defect is named: the wagon's unit number, a dash and the defect's number on that wagon, for example 57408L-3. A wagon has one run of numbers, 1, 2, 3 and so on, shared by its cracks, damage, access structures and prior repairs.","defects",B.x)
B.afG=new A.cq("Grown","The status of a defect that a later inspection found had grown.","defect-page",B.x)
B.afx=new A.cq("No change","The status of a defect that a later inspection found unchanged.","defects",B.x)
B.afl=new A.cq("Missed","The status of a defect that an inspection could not re-inspect; it keeps the severity it was last seen with, and while it has one it is still a current defect.","defects",B.x)
B.af6=new A.cq("Stabilised","The status of a crack that has been held, for example by a crack arrest, but is still there, so it stays a current defect; on the [[Repaired]] page the same word marks a repair recorded with a stabilising action.","repairs",B.x)
B.afJ=new A.cq("Repaired","The status of a defect that has been repaired: it leaves the current counts, is not carried to the next inspection, and is listed on the [[Repaired]] page.","repairs",B.x)
B.afo=new A.cq("Re-cracked","A stabilised crack that has cracked again: the new crack is recorded as a defect of its own at the same place, linked to the stabilised one.","defect-page",B.x)
B.afg=new A.cq("Action taken","What was done to stabilise or repair a defect, such as a crack arrest or a full repair, recorded with the repair.","repairs",B.x)
B.afc=new A.cq("Not inspected","Something an inspection could not look at: a missed defect, a missed area, or a location marked not inspected.","dashboard",B.x)
B.afy=new A.cq("Prior defect","A defect from an earlier inspection of the wagon that the inspection you are recording has not updated yet.","workspace",B.d2)
B.afA=new A.cq("Prior repair","A record of an earlier repair that has not cracked, pinned on a view for reference; it is not a defect, and nothing has to be updated for it.","workspace",B.x)
B.af5=new A.cq("Hot spot","A view of one model, ranked by how many defects are recorded on it.","hotspots",B.x)
B.afH=new A.cq("Crack map","A view's drawing with a pin for each defect recorded on it.","hotspots",B.x)
B.afC=new A.cq("Most Severe","On [[Wagon Health]], a wagon's worst current defect: its severity and that defect's status.","health",B.x)
B.afd=new A.cq("Severity matrix","A table, for one company and one asset type, that suggests a crack's severity from its location type, depth and length; the inspector can change the suggestion, and a lower one needs a reason.","mgmt-thresholds",B.x)
B.afB=new A.cq("Suggested severity","The severity the form fills in for a crack as you enter it, from the severity matrix or a specific threshold; you can choose another, and a lower one needs a reason.","workspace",B.d2)
B.aft=new A.cq("Specific threshold","A rule that sets the severity of a crack at one location, ahead of the severity matrix there: it covers the crack types and depth classes you choose, and a band of lengths.","mgmt-thresholds",B.x)
B.afq=new A.cq("Below suggested severity","The mark on a defect that is graded lower than its thresholds suggest: the severity matrix, or an active specific threshold, gives a crack of its length a higher severity than the defect has.","mgmt-thresholds",B.x)
B.afz=new A.cq("Scope","A named set of views of one model and component; the scope chosen when an inspection is created sets which views it covers.","mgmt-scopes",B.x)
B.afa=new A.cq("Custom","In place of a stored scope: the views were picked by hand for that one inspection.","mgmt-scopes",B.x)
B.aff=new A.cq("Retired","Taken out of use without being deleted: a retired scope is no longer offered for new inspections, and it can be restored.","mgmt-scopes",B.x)
B.afK=new A.cq("Owner company","The company that owns the wagons: a scope or a threshold belongs to one owner company and applies only to that company's wagons.","mgmt-scopes",B.x)
B.afs=new A.cq("Published","The last status of an inspection: recording has finished, and only a WQMS admin can reopen it.","inspection-page",B.x)
B.af8=new A.cq("Automatic notification","An email sent to a person when an inspection is published and it records a new, grown or higher-severity defect at or above the severity chosen for them in [[Notifications]].","mgmt-notifications",B.x)
B.afp=new A.cq("Optional notification","An email sent to a person only if the inspector chooses to send it when publishing an inspection, with a comment if they like; set up in [[Notifications]].","mgmt-notifications",B.x)
B.afh=new A.cq("View only","What the top bar shows for an account that can look but not change anything, such as a Viewer's.","start-roles",B.x)
B.afj=new A.cq("Inspector","A role for people who inspect wagons in the Wagon Inspector tablet app, at the sites they are given; a login that is only an inspector's cannot sign in to the dashboard.","start-roles",B.x)
B.afe=new A.cq("Reliability user","The person named when an inspection is signed off: an active name in the Reliability category of [[Inspectors]], or an active person with a login whose role is Admin or Reliability.","mgmt-users",B.x)
B.afk=new A.cq("Shared tablet login","One login for a tablet that several people use: each picks their own name, from [[Inspectors]] in Users.","mgmt-users",B.x)
B.af9=new A.cq("WQMS admin","A member of the WQMS team, which supports the dashboard: a WQMS admin sees every client's wagons and replies to the requests sent from [[User Support]].","mgmt-support",B.x)
B.afL=new A.cq("Client","A company whose wagons the dashboard holds; the client switcher in the top bar narrows every page to one client.","mgmt-clients",B.co)
B.afi=new A.cq("All clients","The client switcher's choice that shows every client's wagons together; some Management tabs then ask you to pick one client.","start-navigation",B.co)
